From: y-o-o-z <136268860+y-o-o-z@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 21:02:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] local: connect to erssi over its Unix socket
 (irssiConnection.socketPath)

erssi Shellter Edition can listen on a Unix socket instead of a TCP port
(/set fe_web_socket ~/.erssi/fe-web.sock). On a shared box the loopback
port is open to every local user; the socket is 0600 and erssi refuses
connections from other users' processes.

irssiConnection.socketPath (optional, set in the user's file) makes Nexus
connect over that socket instead of host:port. "~/" is the home
directory and a relative path is relative to ~/.erssi, as in erssi.
host and port stay in the file: passwordEncrypted is encrypted with them
as salt, and the settings page keeps saving them as before.

Over the socket nothing else changes: TLS with the same certificate pin
(the default ~/.erssi/fe-web-cert.pem applies, a Unix socket always
means an erssi on this machine), the certificate checked for the name
"localhost" (it is in erssi's certificate), the password in the
Authorization header and AES-256-GCM on top. ws has no wss over a Unix
socket ("ws+unix:" is plain), so the WebSocket is opened for
wss://localhost/ with a createConnection that calls tls.connect() with
"path": ws passes its TLS options (ca, rejectUnauthorized, versions)
through unchanged.

The connection test in the settings uses the stored socketPath as well,
the journal default (~/.erssi/journal) applies to a socket like to a
local host, and log lines name the connection unix:<path>.
